{"content":[{"c":["ELASAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Priest of Pashhur’s clan who obeyed Ezra’s exhortation to divorce his pagan wife after the exile (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.22","r":"Ezra.10.22","rawR":"Ezra.10.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.22","value":"Ezra.10.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 10:22"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Shaphan’s son and King Zedekiah’s envoy to King Nebuchadnezzar of Babylon. On his trip to Babylon, Elasah also carried a letter of encouragement from the prophet Jeremiah to the Jewish exiles there (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.29.3","r":"Jer.29.3","rawR":"Jer.29.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.29.3","value":"Jer.29.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 29:3"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Elasah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Ezr 10:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.10.22","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.10.22","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.10.22"},{"anchorText":"Jer 29:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.29.3","rawQueryValue":"Jer.29.3","sourceRefExact":"Jer.29.3"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"cf746d69aca54085274754a1a469cbd153f9a58921c6dee0c001089f0ec9e7ba","sourceItemName":"Elasah","sourceItemOrder":58,"sourceMember":"Articles/E.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Elasah","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Elasah","title":"Elasah","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}